A||||11||Sootah||Best way to go a hella long distance to pick up a car?||||5||
Z||000000||Sootah||09-25-2001||01:14 AM||||As of right now this is a hypothetical question. I havent finalised on any car yet, but since there isn't shìt around here it is evident that I will have to go quite a ways for the right car. So, how should I do this? Rent a car, and drop it off in the Fieros location? Fly there? Bus (ugh)? I don't have any friends that are going to want to go that far to just have me pick up a car. I could maybe convince one of them to take me about 300 miles. I'm 90% sure that anything I end up getting will be further away than that.<P>Thanx now,<BR>-<B><I>Sootah</I></B><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sootah__Nuclear_Happy_Face_Sig.jpg">  <BR><sup><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I></sup> <BR><sup><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter</sup>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Philphine||09-25-2001||02:26 AM||||i've done greyhound a couple of times to get cars. once 300mls (louisville ky. to coloumbus oh. if i,m not mixing up ohio cities. the one at the top). didn't make it home and ended up leaving the car and having it towed later. the second time about 150mls. (lou. to a city just west of indy.) that time i arranged to rent a uhaul and tow dolly once i got there and towed it back. worked out much better.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroLisa||09-25-2001||02:34 AM||||I picked up my GT from Louisiana when I was living in northern Ohio- I just flew down there Friday night, started driving right after my flight landed (cars owner picked me up from the airport) and drove all day Sat and Sun. Fun times. Actually considering I bought it sight unseen, I'm pretty lucky it made a 1000 mile drive in like 2 days!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTMike||09-25-2001||03:29 AM||||i kinda did the same thing i didn't buy it sight unseen but i flew to Las Vegas.  i met him there looked the car over took it for a drive and gave him the money. and drove back to Ft collins colorado.   well on the way home  the good old check engine light comes on. i was peeing my pants thinking it was something major.  back then i didn't know squat about fieros.   it made it back ok.  and it was the egr tube.   read up on stuff to check on when looking the car over.  and get a manual before you start driveing.  mine only had 43,000 miles on it so i had no troubble.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Nashco||09-25-2001||04:26 AM||||I rode the greyhound about 400 miles to get my car.  I got it off ebay, and saw a ton of pictures and asked a ton of questions before bidding.  I checked everything over (thank god...just because you change the oil every 3k doesn't mean you don't have to check it!) and got on my way.  The car made it fine, and has still been going 5k more without but a minor incident that didn't leave me stranded.  The 12 hour greyhound ride sucked...bad...but it was super cheap and well worth it in the long run.  Once it's over it's not so bad <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-25-2001||05:02 AM||||You couldn't pay me to fly right now.  Hop on a bus.  If you have any friends at a local college, maybe they could post something about needing a ride home for the holidays?||||reg||1
Z||000006||AusFiero||09-25-2001||06:27 AM||||I bought my GT sight unseen and flew 1800kms to pick it up. Made it home without a hitch. I am leaving on Thursday to pick up the new one. a bit closer this time. Only 1000 kms away  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> Then I just realised one major point...Oh sh!t. I have booked a plane ticket and I don't even know if I am allowed to fly. Time to ring my neurosurgeon on his "emergency" 24 7 number. Well a Fiero is an emergency isn't it?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000007||Jake_Dragon||09-25-2001||06:53 AM||||Fly, prices are at an all time low.<BR>If you do have trouble it would be a good time to kick some a**  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<BR>I would probably look into the car dolly as well, but you should be pretty safe flying.||||reg||1
Z||000008||NEPTUNE||09-25-2001||09:13 AM||||A warning to anyone who wants to ship a car- CAR HAULERS ARE NOT REGULATED  by any US or state agency. If the car is damaged in shipping, you are at the mercy of the integrity of the trucker. Be sure to ask for references and check them out! ||||reg||4
Z||000009||rogergarrison||09-25-2001||12:44 PM||||i wouldnt drive a strange car more than a few hundred miles. Take a comfy car or truck with a borrowed or rented trailer or tow dolly to bring it back. May take longer but far less chance of a problem. What if trans or clutch quits 1500 miles away. youll have to leave it and pay inflated repair prices since your from out of town.||||reg||1
